WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.240
A traveller's journal that was

2
00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.900
never kept, around words that

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.450
were truly spoken.

4
00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:09.665
Who sails across an ocean to sit

5
00:00:09.665 --> 00:00:11.665
on a hard bench and listen to

6
00:00:11.665 --> 00:00:14.715
speeches? I do, it seems.

7
00:00:15.385 --> 00:00:18.755
Chicago is all lamps and crowds.

8
00:00:19.321 --> 00:00:21.801
Today a monk from India rose to

9
00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.381
speak at the Parliament of

10
00:00:23.381 --> 00:00:26.061
Religions. His first words were

11
00:00:26.061 --> 00:00:29.181
plain: Sisters and Brothers of

12
00:00:29.181 --> 00:00:30.051
America.

13
00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:32.590
He thanked us in the name of

14
00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:34.910
the most ancient order of monks,

15
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.270
and of the mother of religions.

16
00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.310
His land, he said, had sheltered

17
00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.760
the persecuted of every faith.

18
00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.250
Then he gave us a hymn known

19
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.730
since his boyhood:

20
00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.250
as different streams, having

21
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.630
their sources in different

22
00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.050
places, all mingle their water

23
00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:57.410
in the sea, so, O Lord, the

24
00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.250
different paths all lead to

25
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:00.050
Thee.

26
00:01:00.389 --> 00:01:01.989
He spoke sharply of

27
00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:04.609
sectarianism, bigotry and

28
00:01:04.609 --> 00:01:07.289
fanaticism, and hoped the bell

29
00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:08.989
that tolled that morning would

30
00:01:08.989 --> 00:01:10.569
be the death knell of all

31
00:01:10.569 --> 00:01:11.919
fanaticism.

32
00:01:12.342 --> 00:01:14.202
I walked home under the lamps

33
00:01:14.202 --> 00:01:16.362
with a pencil stub and one

34
00:01:16.362 --> 00:01:20.422
thought: many paths, one sea.

35
00:01:20.422 --> 00:01:22.824
Yours, a traveller.

36
00:01:23.724 --> 00:01:25.324
For GS1 and GS4:

37
00:01:25.324 --> 00:01:28.404
the address of 11 September 1893

38
00:01:28.404 --> 00:01:30.604
argued for tolerance and

39
00:01:30.604 --> 00:01:32.784
universal acceptance, against

40
00:01:32.784 --> 00:01:35.334
sectarianism and fanaticism.

41
00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:37.787
Many paths.

42
00:01:37.787 --> 00:01:39.469
One sea.
